---
import AppShell from '../../layouts/AppShell.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { ORGANIZATION_REF, SOCIAL_IMAGE_URL, WEBSITE_REF } from '../../lib/seo';

export const prerender = true;

const title = 'Custom AI Agent Development Services | Neil Busque';
const description = 'Custom AI agents that work inside your CRM, inbox, calendar, and database, with clear permissions, approval steps, and direct access to the builder.';
const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/services/ai-agent-development';

const service = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  '@id': `${canonical}#service`,
  name: 'AI Agent Development Services',
  url: canonical,
  image: SOCIAL_IMAGE_URL,
  provider: ORGANIZATION_REF,
  brand: ORGANIZATION_REF,
  isPartOf: WEBSITE_REF,
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@id': `${canonical}#webpage` },
  areaServed: ['New Jersey', 'New York', 'New York City', 'United States', 'Remote'],
  serviceType: ['AI agent development', 'LLM application development', 'MCP tool integration', 'AI automation'],
  description,
};
---
<AppShell title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} active="services">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <Breadcrumb items={[
      { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
      { name: 'Services', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/services' },
      { name: 'AI Agent Development', url: canonical },
    ]} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(service)} />
  </Fragment>

  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="idx">&#8727;</span> Services &#183; AI Agents</p>
    <h1>AI agent development <span class="accent">services</span>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I build agents that work inside the tools your team already uses. They can answer leads, update the CRM, run research, and draft a reply for a person to approve.</p>
  </header>

  <article class="article-page">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What an AI agent actually is</h2>
      <p>A useful agent is more than a chat window. It reads a situation, chooses the next step, and uses a small set of tools to complete the job. The important difference is action: a chatbot answers, while an agent can update the systems where the work lives.</p>

      <h2>Agents I build</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Inbox and lead agents.</strong> Read what came in, classify it, look the person up, draft the reply, log it, and escalate the ones that need you.</li>
        <li><strong>CRM agents.</strong> Keep records clean, enrich contacts, move deals on real signals rather than on someone remembering.</li>
        <li><strong>Research agents.</strong> Pull sources on a schedule, summarize, and hand you a brief instead of a tab graveyard.</li>
        <li><strong>Ops agents.</strong> Watch for a condition, do the multi-step thing that follows, and tell you when it could not.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The stack</h2>
      <p>I usually build on Claude and connect the agent through MCP. That gives it controlled access to a CRM, inbox, calendar, or database without hard-wiring every tool into one app. The permissions and the shape of the job matter more than the model name.</p>

      <h2>Guardrails, because agents fail</h2>
      <p>Every agent needs a clear boundary. Reads can be broad when the data is safe. Writes stay limited to the job. Anything a customer will see should wait for approval unless you decide otherwise. The goal is not pretending the agent will never make a mistake. It is making mistakes visible, reversible, and cheap.</p>

      <h2>How the work runs</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>One call to find the job.</strong> Which repeated decision are we handing over, and what is it allowed to touch.</li>
        <li><strong>I scope it before building.</strong> You see the boundaries in writing first.</li>
        <li><strong>I build and wire it in.</strong> Into your actual systems, not a demo environment.</li>
        <li><strong>You watch it run.</strong> With logs, so you can see what it did and why.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Who you are working with</h2>
      <p>You work with me directly from the first call through launch. I am Neil Busque, based in Elizabeth, New Jersey, and I work across the NJ and NYC metro and remotely across the United States. I shipped more than 40 web apps, agents, and automations in 2026, including a CRM with agents built into it. See <a href="/work">the work</a> and read <a href="/guides/build-ai-agent-claude-code">how I build agents</a> before we talk.</p>

      <h2>Start here</h2>
      <p>Tell me the decision you want handed over and I will tell you whether an agent is the right shape for it. <a href="/contact">Send me the problem</a>, or read about <a href="/services/ai-automation-services">AI automation services</a> more broadly.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="hire-cta v8-card">
    <span class="eyebrow">The guarantee</span>
    <p class="guarantee">I keep working until you are proud of it. If I am not the right fit, I will tell you on the first call.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn-sun" href="/contact">Tell me what you need</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="https://wa.me/19083164140?text=Hi%20Neil%2C%20I%20want%20to%20talk%20about%20a%20build">Or message on WhatsApp</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</AppShell>
